(stmts#Hypothesis: in the item pool (core/itempool), some interleaving of two pool workers and the
 job's own thread (the caller, which runs items itself and takes the results strictly in order),
 one item raising, a cancel, and the caller's `take` raising makes a batch hang (a lost wakeup on
 the batch's `ready` or the pool's `work`), run an item twice, take one out of order, hold more
 than Win results, return while an item still runs, or leave a worker unjoined after shutdown.
 Source: src/viewSEG/core/itempool.nim. One pool lock guards every batch. Worker (workerLoop):
 lock; leave when stopping; hand out the next item of the first batch where Startable (reserving
 it: inc next and inc inFlight in the same region) else wait on `work`; unlock; run the item
 (the wrapper catches CatchableError into an ItemFailure, a Defect ends the process); lock; slot
 full, dec inFlight, broadcast `ready`; a worker that saw the cancel sets the batch's stop.
 Caller (parallelItems): lock; stop -> drain; slot `taken` full -> take it out, inc taken,
 broadcast `work`; unlock; look at the cancel; take(i) (may raise); Startable -> hand an item to
 itself, run it, place it (no wake); else wait on `ready`. The drain: lock, stop, broadcast
 `work`, wait on `ready` while inFlight > 0, unregister.
 Variables: wpc per worker 0 check, 1 waits on work, 2 runs, 3 places, 4 exited, 6 waits for
 window room at place time (Mut 8), 8 read the next item without taking it (Mut 4); cur: the
 worker's item; obs: it saw the cancel; wk: woken; next, taken: handout and take-out counters;
 st per item 0 new, 1 running, 2 placed, 3 taken; stop 0 none, 1 cancel, 2 take raised, 3 all
 taken (the drain); cx: a cancel asked for; fails, traises: failures left; cpc caller 0 check,
 1 waits on ready, 2 runs its item, 3 take (unlocked), 4 drain, 5 drain-wait, 6 returned, 7
 places its own item, 8 decided to wait with the lock released (Mut 3), 9 waits for room at
 place time (Mut 8); ccur, cwk: the caller's item, woken; pstop: Jobs shutdown; err 1 an item
 handed out twice; ovl, stopWoke, drainWaited: witness history.
 Switches: Fix (true: the caller runs items itself; false: it only takes, so workers must run
 them); Mut 0 none; 1 a worker's place does not wake the caller; 2 a take-out does not broadcast
 `work`; 3 the caller tests and waits in two lock regions; 4 the worker's handout is a read and
 a later increment; 5 the drain does not wait for inFlight 0; 6 the worker's wait ignores the
 shutdown; 7 a worker's exception escapes the wrapper (the worker dies); 8 the window is checked
 when placing, not when handing out.
 Witness 1: item 1 placed while item 0 ran and the run completed whole; 2: a stop woke a waiter
 and the batch returned after a cancel; 3: take raised while a worker ran and the drain waited.
 Run: tlacheck.py docs/models/itempool.nif --expect:pass (70670 states), then with
 --live:Returned,Joined --fair:Worker1,Worker2,Caller,Shutdown for liveness (pass).
 Expected: base passes safety and liveness; the three witnesses fail; Fix=(false) passes;
 Mut 1 3 6 7 fail liveness (exit 3), Mut 4 5 8 fail safety (exit 2; Mut 8 as err 3, more than Win
 results held, before it can hang); Mut 2 passes with Fix true and fails liveness with
 Fix=(false) (the caller running items is what makes the missing wake-up safe).#
  (variables :wpc.0. :cur.0. :obs.0. :wk.0. :next.0. :taken.0. :st.0. :stop.0. :cx.0. :fails.0.
    :traises.0. :cpc.0. :ccur.0. :cwk.0. :pstop.0. :err.0. :ovl.0. :stopWoke.0. :drainWaited.0.)
  (assign Fix.0. (true))
  (assign Mut.0. 0)
  (assign Witness.0. 0)
  (assign N.0. 4)
  (assign Win.0. 2)
  (assign MaxIn.0. 3)
  (assign Workers.0. (set 1 2))
  (assign Items.0. (range 0 3))

  (def :Init.0.
    (and (prime wpc.0. (funof :v.0 Workers.0. 0)) (prime cur.0. (funof :v.0 Workers.0. 0))
      (prime obs.0. (funof :v.0 Workers.0. (false))) (prime wk.0. (funof :v.0 Workers.0. (false)))
      (prime next.0. 0) (prime taken.0. 0) (prime st.0. (funof :i.0 Items.0. 0))
      (prime stop.0. 0) (prime cx.0. (false)) (prime fails.0. 1) (prime traises.0. 1)
      (prime cpc.0. 0) (prime ccur.0. 0) (prime cwk.0. (false)) (prime pstop.0. (false))
      (prime err.0. 0) (prime ovl.0. (false)) (prime stopWoke.0. (false))
      (prime drainWaited.0. (false))))

  (def :Wpc.0. (apply wpc.0. Me.0.))
  (def :Cur.0. (apply cur.0. Me.0.))
  (def :Running.0. (eq err.0. 0))
  (def :InFlight.0. (card (setcomp :i.0 Items.0. (eq (apply st.0. i.0) 1))))
  (def :Held.0. (card (setcomp :i.0 Items.0. (or (eq (apply st.0. i.0) 1) (eq (apply st.0. i.0) 2)))))
  (def :Startable.0.#Startable(b), pool lock held, the batch registered (cpc < 6)#
    (and (lt cpc.0. 6) (eq stop.0. 0) (lt next.0. N.0.)
      (or (eq Mut.0. 8) (lt next.0. (plus taken.0. Win.0.)))
      (lt InFlight.0. MaxIn.0.)))
  (def :WaitersOnWork.0.#a broadcast on `work`: every worker waiting on it is woken#
    (funof :v.0 Workers.0. (or (apply wk.0. v.0)
      (or (eq (apply wpc.0. v.0) 1) (eq (apply wpc.0. v.0) 6)))))
  (def :CallerWaits.0. (or (eq cpc.0. 1) (or (eq cpc.0. 5) (eq cpc.0. 9))))
  (def :AnyWaiting.0.
    (or CallerWaits.0. (exists :v.0 Workers.0. (or (eq (apply wpc.0. v.0) 1) (eq (apply wpc.0. v.0) 6)))))

  (def :WCheck.0.#workerLoop, lock held: exit when stopping; hand out (reserve) or wait on work#
    (and Running.0. (eq Wpc.0. 0)
      (if (and pstop.0. (not (eq Mut.0. 6)))
        (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 4)))
        (if Startable.0.
          (if (eq Mut.0. 4)
            (and (prime cur.0. (except cur.0. (mapsto Me.0. next.0.)))
              (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 8))))
            (and (prime cur.0. (except cur.0. (mapsto Me.0. next.0.)))
              (prime st.0. (except st.0. (mapsto next.0. 1)))
              (prime err.0. (if (eq (apply st.0. next.0.) 0) 0 1))
              (prime next.0. (plus next.0. 1))
              (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 2)))))
          (and (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 1)))
            (prime wk.0. (except wk.0. (mapsto Me.0. (false)))))))))

  (def :WTakeB.0.#Mut 4 only: the increment in a later lock region, from the number read before#
    (and Running.0. (eq Wpc.0. 8)
      (prime err.0. (if (eq (apply st.0. Cur.0.) 0) 0 1))
      (prime st.0. (except st.0. (mapsto Cur.0. 1)))
      (prime next.0. (plus Cur.0. 1))
      (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 2)))))

  (def :WWake.0.#woken from work: test again under the lock#
    (and Running.0. (eq Wpc.0. 1) (apply wk.0. Me.0.)
      (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 0)))
      (prime wk.0. (except wk.0. (mapsto Me.0. (false))))))

  (def :WRun.0.#the item, unlocked: ok or an exception; the cancel hook is read once#
    (and Running.0. (eq Wpc.0. 2)
      (prime obs.0. (except obs.0. (mapsto Me.0. cx.0.)))
      (or
        (and (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 3))) (unchanged fails.0.))
        (and (gt fails.0. 0) (prime fails.0. (minus fails.0. 1))
          (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. (if (eq Mut.0. 7) 4 3))))))))

  (def :WPlace.0.#lock: slot full, dec inFlight, a seen cancel sets stop, broadcast ready (and work)#
    (and Running.0. (eq Wpc.0. 3)
      (if (and (eq Mut.0. 8) (ge Cur.0. (plus taken.0. Win.0.)))
        (and (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 6)))
          (prime wk.0. (except wk.0. (mapsto Me.0. (false)))))
        (and (prime st.0. (except st.0. (mapsto Cur.0. 2)))
          (prime ovl.0. (or ovl.0.
            (exists :j.0 Items.0. (and (lt j.0 Cur.0.) (eq (apply st.0. j.0) 1)))))
          (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 0)))
          (if (and (apply obs.0. Me.0.) (eq stop.0. 0))
            (and (prime stop.0. 1) (prime wk.0. WaitersOnWork.0.)
              (prime stopWoke.0. (or stopWoke.0. AnyWaiting.0.)))
            (unchanged stop.0. wk.0. stopWoke.0.))
          (prime cwk.0. (if (eq Mut.0. 1) cwk.0. (or cwk.0. CallerWaits.0.)))))))

  (def :WWake6.0.#Mut 8 only: woken after a take-out, place again#
    (and Running.0. (eq Wpc.0. 6) (apply wk.0. Me.0.)
      (prime wpc.0. (except wpc.0. (mapsto Me.0. 3)))
      (prime wk.0. (except wk.0. (mapsto Me.0. (false))))))

  (def :WorkerActs.0. (or WCheck.0. WTakeB.0. WWake.0. WRun.0. WPlace.0. WWake6.0.))
  (def :Worker1.0. (let (bind :Me.0. 1) WorkerActs.0.))
  (def :Worker2.0. (let (bind :Me.0. 2) WorkerActs.0.))

  (def :CCheck.0.#parallelItems loop, lock held: stop -> drain; slot full -> take out; startable -> run it; wait#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 0)
      (if (or (not (eq stop.0. 0)) (ge taken.0. N.0.))
        (prime cpc.0. 4)
        (if (eq (apply st.0. taken.0.) 2)
          (and (prime st.0. (except st.0. (mapsto taken.0. 3))) (prime ccur.0. taken.0.)
            (prime taken.0. (plus taken.0. 1))
            (prime wk.0. (if (eq Mut.0. 2) wk.0. WaitersOnWork.0.))
            (prime cpc.0. 3))
          (if (and Fix.0. Startable.0.)
            (and (prime ccur.0. next.0.) (prime st.0. (except st.0. (mapsto next.0. 1)))
              (prime err.0. (if (eq (apply st.0. next.0.) 0) 0 1))
              (prime next.0. (plus next.0. 1)) (prime cpc.0. 2))
            (and (prime cpc.0. (if (eq Mut.0. 3) 8 1)) (prime cwk.0. (false))))))))

  (def :CWake.0.#woken from ready: test again#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 1) cwk.0. (prime cpc.0. 0) (prime cwk.0. (false))))

  (def :CBlock.0.#Mut 3 only: the wait, in a second lock region after the test#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 8) (prime cpc.0. 1)))

  (def :CRun.0.#the caller's own item, unlocked: ok or an exception (caught by the wrapper)#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 2)
      (or (and (prime cpc.0. 7) (unchanged fails.0.))
        (and (gt fails.0. 0) (prime fails.0. (minus fails.0. 1)) (prime cpc.0. 7)))))

  (def :CPlace.0.#lock: slot full, dec inFlight; the caller wakes no one, it looks again itself#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 7)
      (if (and (eq Mut.0. 8) (ge ccur.0. (plus taken.0. Win.0.)))
        (and (prime cpc.0. 9) (prime cwk.0. (false)))
        (and (prime st.0. (except st.0. (mapsto ccur.0. 2)))
          (prime ovl.0. (or ovl.0.
            (exists :j.0 Items.0. (and (lt j.0 ccur.0.) (eq (apply st.0. j.0) 1)))))
          (prime cpc.0. 0)))))

  (def :CWake9.0.#Mut 8 only: woken, place again#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 9) cwk.0. (prime cpc.0. 7) (prime cwk.0. (false))))

  (def :CTake.0.#unlocked: the cancel is looked at, then take(i), which may raise#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 3)
      (or
        (and cx.0. (prime stop.0. (if (eq stop.0. 0) 1 stop.0.))
          (prime wk.0. WaitersOnWork.0.) (prime cpc.0. 4))
        (and (not cx.0.) (gt traises.0. 0) (prime traises.0. (minus traises.0. 1))
          (prime stop.0. (if (eq stop.0. 0) 2 stop.0.)) (prime wk.0. WaitersOnWork.0.)
          (prime cpc.0. 4))
        (and (not cx.0.) (prime err.0. (if (eq stop.0. 2) 5 0)) (prime cpc.0. 0)))))

  (def :CDrain.0.#finally, lock: stop, broadcast work, wait on ready while inFlight > 0, unregister#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 4)
      (prime stop.0. (if (eq stop.0. 0) 3 stop.0.))
      (prime wk.0. WaitersOnWork.0.)
      (if (or (eq Mut.0. 5) (eq InFlight.0. 0))
        (prime cpc.0. 6)
        (and (prime cpc.0. 5) (prime cwk.0. (false))
          (prime drainWaited.0. (or drainWaited.0. (eq stop.0. 2)))))))

  (def :CDrainWake.0.#woken from ready in the drain: test inFlight again#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 5) cwk.0. (prime cpc.0. 4) (prime cwk.0. (false))))

  (def :Caller.0. (or CCheck.0. CWake.0. CBlock.0. CRun.0. CPlace.0. CWake9.0. CTake.0.
    CDrain.0. CDrainWake.0.))

  (def :Cancel.0.#the user cancels, at any time before the batch returns (no fairness)#
    (and Running.0. (not cx.0.) (not (eq cpc.0. 6)) (prime cx.0. (true))))

  (def :Shutdown.0.#Jobs.stop after the batch returned: stopping, broadcast work#
    (and Running.0. (eq cpc.0. 6) (not pstop.0.) (prime pstop.0. (true))
      (prime wk.0. WaitersOnWork.0.)))

  (def :Next.0. (or Worker1.0. Worker2.0. Caller.0. Cancel.0. Shutdown.0.))

  (def :Safe.0.#no double handout; at most Win results held; at most MaxIn running; the batch
 returns only with no item running; taken items form a prefix, all taken; a normal end took all#
    (and (eq err.0. 0)
      (le Held.0. Win.0.)
      (le InFlight.0. MaxIn.0.)
      (forall :i.0 Items.0. (implies (lt i.0 taken.0.) (eq (apply st.0. i.0) 3)))
      (forall :i.0 Items.0. (implies (ge i.0 next.0.) (eq (apply st.0. i.0) 0)))
      (implies (eq cpc.0. 6) (eq InFlight.0. 0))
      (implies (and (eq cpc.0. 6) (eq stop.0. 3)) (eq taken.0. N.0.))))

  (def :Returned.0. (or (eq cpc.0. 6) (not (eq err.0. 0))))
  (def :Joined.0. (or (not (eq err.0. 0))
    (and pstop.0. (forall :v.0 Workers.0. (eq (apply wpc.0. v.0) 4)))))
  (def :Reached1.0. (and (eq cpc.0. 6) (eq stop.0. 3) ovl.0.))
  (def :Reached2.0. (and (eq cpc.0. 6) (eq stop.0. 1) stopWoke.0.))
  (def :Reached3.0. (and (eq cpc.0. 6) (eq stop.0. 2) drainWaited.0.))

  (spec (always-stutter Init.0. Next.0. (tuple wpc.0. cur.0. obs.0. wk.0. next.0. taken.0. st.0.
    stop.0. cx.0. fails.0. traises.0. cpc.0. ccur.0. cwk.0. pstop.0. err.0. ovl.0. stopWoke.0.
    drainWaited.0.)))
  (check (if (eq Witness.0. 1) (not Reached1.0.)
    (if (eq Witness.0. 2) (not Reached2.0.)
      (if (eq Witness.0. 3) (not Reached3.0.) Safe.0.)))))
